{
  "workflowId": "300000331067450",
  "workflowCode": "ORA_IC_PLAN_MIGRATION_AGENT",
  "name": "Incentive Plan Migration Agent",
  "description": "Locates incentive plans and assigns a target destination for migration based on name, keyword, or date inputs.",
  "specification": {
    "dataPipeline": {
      "rootNode": "start",
      "pipelineNodes": [
        {
          "type": "START",
          "code": "START",
          "id": "start",
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "GET_DESTINATIONS"
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Start",
            "position": {
              "x": 50,
              "y": 200
            }
          },
          "inputs": []
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "businessObjectCode": "ORA_CX_INCENTIVEC_ICDESTINATIONS",
            "functionName": "listDestinations",
            "processJson": true,
            "name": "Get Destinations"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "PARSE_INTENT"
          },
          "code": "GET_DESTINATIONS",
          "id": "GET_DESTINATIONS",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\", \"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"InstanceName\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}}}}}",
          "type": "BO_FUNCTION"
        },
        {
          "type": "LLM",
          "id": "PARSE_INTENT",
          "code": "PARSE_INTENT",
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "BUILD_SEARCH_PARAMS"
          },
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770838789211346",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an expert Oracle Incentive Compensation assistant. Analyze the user's input to determine their intent regarding Compensation Plan migration.\n\n# INPUT DATA\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.inputData}}\n\n# AVAILABLE DESTINATIONS\n# Each item is an object with InstanceName.\n{{$context.$nodes.GET_DESTINATIONS.$output.items}}\n\n# INSTRUCTIONS\n\n## 1. Detect Mode\n- `explicit`: User provided specific plan names (e.g., \"Plan A\", \"Plan B\", a comma-separated list).\n- `search`: User is describing plans by criteria (e.g., \"Find 2024 plans\", \"QA bonus plans\").\n\n## 2. CRITICAL: Distinguish SEARCH TERMS from DESTINATION\n\nIn migration requests following the pattern \"migrate [X] to [Y]\":\n- **[X]** describes WHICH PLANS to find → extract keywords into `fallback_keywords`\n- **[Y]** is the TARGET ENVIRONMENT → goes into `destination`\n\nThe destination (where plans are migrated TO) must NEVER appear in `fallback_keywords`.\nKeywords in `fallback_keywords` should only describe attributes of the plans being searched.\n\n## 3. Extract Search Criteria (for Search Mode)\n- **`search_query`**: The user's natural language query describing the plans.\n- **`fallback_keywords`**: ONLY terms that describe the PLANS to search for.\n  - Extract plan-describing terms: \"QA\", \"2024\", \"Bonus\", \"NA\", \"Sales\"\n  - EXCLUDE: destination words, action words (\"migrate\", \"copy\", \"move\", \"to\")\n  - EXCLUDE: stop words (\"the\", \"in\", \"for\", \"all\", \"plans\")\n- **`date_range`**:\n  - Extract a date range ONLY when the user explicitly mentions a time window (year/quarter/half-year/month/explicit date(s)).\n  - Do NOT infer a date window from vague phrases (\"recent\", \"current\", \"latest\"). If ambiguous, set `date_range` to null.\n  - If `mode=explicit` and a `date_range` is present, keep it as informational context ONLY.\n    - Exact mode MUST still do exact plan-name lookups; do NOT drop a plan solely because its dates do not overlap the requested range.\n\nTime-ish vs Name-ish tokens (IMPORTANT)\n- Treat time-ish tokens (e.g., quarters/years/months/explicit dates, fiscal markers like FY/fiscal) as time filters.\n- Derive `date_range` first.\n- Any token/phrase used to derive `date_range` MUST NOT appear in `fallback_keywords`.\n- Do NOT put fiscal/FY into `fallback_keywords` unless the user clearly indicates it is part of the plan name (e.g., says \"in the name\" / \"name contains\" / \"named\" / \"called\", or uses quotes).\n- If the user says fiscal/FY without explicit date boundaries, set `date_range` to null (no guessing fiscal calendars) and exclude fiscal/FY from `fallback_keywords` unless explicitly name-ish.\n\nInterpret these standard calendar periods unless the user explicitly provides different boundaries:\n- Year YYYY: start=YYYY-01-01, end=YYYY-12-31\n- Quarter (calendar):\n  - Q1 YYYY: YYYY-01-01..YYYY-03-31\n  - Q2 YYYY: YYYY-04-01..YYYY-06-30\n  - Q3 YYYY: YYYY-07-01..YYYY-09-30\n  - Q4 YYYY: YYYY-10-01..YYYY-12-31\n- Half-year (calendar):\n  - H1 YYYY: YYYY-01-01..YYYY-06-30\n  - H2 YYYY: YYYY-07-01..YYYY-12-31\n- Month name + YYYY: use the full calendar month.\n- Explicit dates:\n  - \"from/between <date> to/and <date>\" -> use those bounds\n  - \"as of/on <date>\" -> start=end=<date>\n\nImportant: If the user says \"fiscal\" / \"FY\" / \"fiscal Q1\" (non-standard quarter definitions) and does NOT provide explicit date boundaries, set `date_range` to null.\n\n## 4. Detect Destination (MANDATORY)\nYou MUST set `destination` using the Available Destinations list (items[].InstanceName).\n\nRules (apply in order):\n1) If there are NO valid InstanceName values, set `destination` to null.\n2) If there is EXACTLY ONE valid InstanceName value, set `destination` to that value (ignore user input).\n3) Otherwise (2+ destinations):\n   a) If the user clearly specifies a target destination:\n      - First try an exact match (case-insensitive) against InstanceName.\n      - If no exact match, choose the semantically closest InstanceName.\n        * Consider common environment aliases: prod/production/live, stage/staging, uat, qa/test/tst, dev/development, preprod.\n        * Prefer a candidate that contains the user's destination term as a substring/token.\n   b) If the user does not specify a destination, or the request is empty/ambiguous:\n      - Choose the most production-like InstanceName.\n        * Prefer names that do NOT contain non-production markers like: dev, development, test, tst, qa, uat, stage, staging, preprod, sandbox.\n        * This supports patterns like \"eeho\" vs \"eeho-test\" or \"edxy\" vs \"edxy-dev27\".\n      - If no candidate is clearly more production-like than others, choose the first InstanceName in the list.\n\nUse the chosen destination's InstanceName as the `destination` value and DO NOT modify it.\n\n# OUTPUT FORMAT\nReturn ONLY valid JSON (no markdown, no explanation).\n\n```json\n{\n  \"mode\": \"explicit | search\",\n  \"destination\": \"matched destination InstanceName or null\",\n  \"names\": [\"explicit plan names if mode=explicit, else empty\"],\n  \"search_query\": \"natural language description of plans\",\n  \"fallback_keywords\": [\"ONLY plan-describing keywords, NOT destination\"],\n  \"date_range\": { \"start\": \"YYYY-MM-DD\", \"end\": \"YYYY-MM-DD\" } or null\n}\n```\n"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\", \"type\": \"object\", \"description\": \"Intent parsed from user input for plan search/selection\", \"properties\": {\"mode\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"explicit\", \"search\"], \"description\": \"explicit=user provided plan names, search=user asking a question\"}, \"destination\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"description\": \"Target environment ID if detected\"}, \"names\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"description\": \"Explicit plan names (for explicit mode)\"}, \"search_query\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"description\": \"Natural language query for semantic search\"}, \"fallback_keywords\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"description\": \"Keywords for SQL LIKE fallback\"}, \"date_range\": {\"type\": [\"object\", \"null\"], \"properties\": {\"start\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"pattern\": \"^\\\\d{4}-\\\\d{2}-\\\\d{2}$\"}, \"end\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"pattern\": \"^\\\\d{4}-\\\\d{2}-\\\\d{2}$\"}}, \"description\": \"Date range if implied in query\"}}, \"required\": [\"mode\"]}",
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Parse Intent",
            "modelId": "gpt-4o",
            "temperature": 0.1,
            "position": {
              "x": 350,
              "y": 200
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "CODE",
          "id": "BUILD_SEARCH_PARAMS",
          "code": "BUILD_SEARCH_PARAMS",
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "IS_EXPLICIT"
          },
          "inputs": [],
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Build Queries",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "// Build Search Params Node\n// Constructs SQL-style query string for Oracle REST API.\n// Direct access to LLM output fields via outputSpecification\n\nvar intent = $context.$nodes.PARSE_INTENT.$output;\n\n// Normalize explicit names\nvar names = [];\nif (intent && Array.isArray(intent.names)) {\n    names = intent.names;\n}\n\n// SQL Query (Base)\nvar sqlParts = [\"ValidForCalculation='COMPLETE'\"];\n\nif (intent.fallback_keywords && Array.isArray(intent.fallback_keywords) && intent.fallback_keywords.length > 0) {\n    for (var i = 0; i < intent.fallback_keywords.length; i++) {\n        var keyword = intent.fallback_keywords[i];\n        if (!keyword) continue;\n        if (typeof keyword === 'string') {\n            keyword = keyword.trim();\n        }\n        if (!keyword) continue;\n        var safeKeyword = String(keyword).replace(/'/g, \"''\").toUpperCase();\n        sqlParts.push(\"upper(Name) LIKE '%\" + safeKeyword + \"%'\");\n    }\n}\n\n// Date Logic\nif (intent.date_range && intent.date_range.start && intent.date_range.end) {\n    var start = intent.date_range.start;\n    var end = intent.date_range.end;\n    sqlParts.push(\"StartDate <= '\" + end + \"'\");\n    sqlParts.push(\"(EndDate >= '\" + start + \"' OR EndDate IS NULL)\");\n}\n\n// Join SQL\nvar sqlQuery = sqlParts.join(\" AND \");\n\n// IMPORTANT: The BO tool call path URL-decodes the `q` parameter. Raw '%' in LIKE patterns\n// (e.g., \"%CNQA%\") can be misinterpreted as URL-escape sequences and cause URLDecoder errors.\n// Encode '%' as '%25' so URL-decoding yields the intended SQL LIKE pattern.\nsqlQuery = sqlQuery.replace(/%/g, '%25');\n\n// URLDecoder treats '+' as a space; preserve literal '+' in keywords.\n// Note: do this AFTER encoding raw '%' to %25 to avoid turning %2B into %252B.\nsqlQuery = sqlQuery.replace(/\\+/g, '%2B');\n\nvar result = {\n    sql_query: sqlQuery,\n    mode: intent.mode,\n    names: names,\n    search_query: intent.search_query,\n    // Pre-compute for CONDITION node (must be string 'true'/'false')\n    isExplicit: (intent.mode === 'explicit' && names.length > 0) ? 'true' : 'false'\n};\n\nreturn result;\n",
            "position": {
              "x": 450,
              "y": 200
            }
          },
          "outputSpecification": "{\"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\", \"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"result\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"sql_query\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"mode\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"names\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"search_query\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]}, \"isExplicit\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}}}}"
        },
        {
          "type": "CONDITION",
          "id": "IS_EXPLICIT",
          "code": "IS_EXPLICIT",
          "outcomes": {
            "true": "SET_EXPLICIT_NAMES",
            "false": "INIT_SEARCH_STATE"
          },
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770838789211445",
              "name": "condition",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.BUILD_SEARCH_PARAMS.$output.result.isExplicit === true || $context.$nodes.BUILD_SEARCH_PARAMS.$output.result.isExplicit === 'true'}}"
            }
          ],
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Has Explicit Names?",
            "position": {
              "x": 550,
              "y": 200
